riscv: enable the RoCC extension context for user threads

Rocket-class cores gate custom (RoCC) instructions on sstatus.XS: with the
extension context Off, every accelerator instruction traps as illegal. Mainline
Linux never touches XS - no upstream hart has RoCC state - so userspace cannot
reach accelerators like Gemmini without this. Mark the extension context Initial
for every new user thread, mirroring what start_thread already does for the FPU
via SR_FS_INITIAL. The status field is per-thread (pt_regs) and context-switched
as a whole, so this composes with scheduling; on designs without a RoCC the bit
is inert.

Not upstreamable as-is (upstream would want this keyed on an extension probe),
which is why it lives here - see patches/README.md for the policy.

--- a/arch/riscv/kernel/process.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/kernel/process.c
@@ -145,6 +145,12 @@ void start_thread(struct pt_regs *regs, unsigned long pc,
 	unsigned long sp)
 {
 	regs->status = SR_PIE;
+	/*
+	 * RoCC accelerators (custom instructions) require the extension context
+	 * enabled; without XS every accelerator instruction traps as illegal.
+	 * Inert on harts without a RoCC.
+	 */
+	regs->status |= SR_XS_INITIAL;
 	if (has_fpu()) {
 		regs->status |= SR_FS_INITIAL;
 		/*
